[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m }
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Quirks in the C that the Rust must reproduce (and does)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m These are the places where a natural, idiomatic Rust rewrite would silently
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m diverge. Each is deliberately preserved, and each is pinned by a test.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### 1. The last byte is deleted unconditionally, not "the newline is stripped"
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `s1[strlen(s1)-1] = '\0'` removes the final byte whatever it is. It only looks
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m like newline-stripping because the common case ends in a newline. When the line
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m has no trailing newline (EOF) or was truncated by `fgets`, this deletes a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     55[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **data** byte.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     56[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     57[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - Input `"abc"` (no newline) -> `s1` becomes `"ab"`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     58[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - A 99-byte line fills the buffer with no newline, so the chop leaves 98 bytes.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     59[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     60[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Pinned by `single_line_no_trailing_newline`, `buffer_length_boundaries`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     61[0m:[38;5;10m[49m A mutant that made the chop newline-aware (the "fixed" version) failed 9 tests.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     62[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     63[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### 2. `s[strlen(s)-1]` underflows to index -1 when the string is empty
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     64[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     65[0m:[38;5;10m[49m If `fgets` hits EOF immediately it returns NULL and leaves the buffer as `""`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     66[0m:[38;5;10m[49m so `strlen` is 0 and the index is `(size_t)-1`. This is an out-of-bounds store
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     67[0m:[38;5;10m[49m and formally undefined behavior. It is emulated as a no-op, which was confirmed
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     68[0m:[38;5;10m[49m against the compiled binary rather than assumed:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     69[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     70[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     71[0m:[38;5;10m[49m main:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     72[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   ...          # s1 at rsp+0x00 (100 bytes, 0x00..0x63)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     73[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   lea 0x70(%rsp),%rdi        # s2 at rsp+0x70 (0x70..0xd3)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     74[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   movb $0x0,-0x1(%rsp,%rax,1)   # s1[strlen(s1)-1], rax=0 -> rsp-0x01
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     75[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   movb $0x0,0x6f(%rsp,%rax,1)   # s2[strlen(s2)-1], rax=0 -> rsp+0x6f
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     76[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     77[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     78[0m:[38;5;10m[49m With `rax == 0` the stores land at `rsp-0x01` (below the frame) and `rsp+0x6f`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     79[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (the padding gap between the end of `s1` at `0x63` and the start of `s2` at
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     80[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `0x70`). Neither byte is part of `s1` or `s2`, so neither can affect the printed
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     81[0m:[38;5;10m[49m result. Even had the arrays been adjacent it would remain a no-op: `fgets` never
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     82[0m:[38;5;10m[49m leaves a non-zero byte at index 99 of either buffer, since it writes at most 99
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     83[0m:[38;5;10m[49m bytes plus a NUL terminator.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     84[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     85[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Reached by empty input, `"\n"`, `"\n\n"`, and any input with fewer than two
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     86[0m:[38;5;10m[49m non-empty lines. Pinned by `empty_and_near_empty_input`. A mutant that performed
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     87[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the chop unconditionally (panicking on the empty case) failed 8 tests.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     88[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     89[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### 3. `fgets` does not read across newlines, and a long line spills into `s2`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     90[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     91[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `fgets(buf, 100, stdin)` consumes at most 99 bytes and stops after a newline.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     92[0m:[38;5;10m[49m A first line longer than 99 bytes is truncated, and **the remainder of that same
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     93[0m:[38;5;10m[49m line is what the second `fgets` reads** — so `s2` is filled from the tail of
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     94[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `s1`'s own line, not from a separate line.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     95[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     96[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - 149 `a`/`b` bytes on one line: `s1` = 99 `a`s (chopped to 98), `s2` = the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     97[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   50 `b`s (chopped to 49).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     98[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - 100 `a`s + newline: `s1` = 98 `a`s after the chop, `s2` = `"a"`, so `strcspn`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     99[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   returns 0, not 100.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    100[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    101[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Pinned by `long_line_spills_into_second_fgets`, `buffer_length_boundaries`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    102[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `reject_byte_at_every_index_near_boundary`, `reject_set_at_length_boundary`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    103[0m:[38;5;10m[49m A mutant reading 100 bytes instead of 99 failed 6 tests.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    104[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    105[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### 4. NUL bytes in the input truncate the effective strings
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    106[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    107[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `fgets` copies NUL bytes into the buffer verbatim, but `strlen` and `strcspn`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    108[0m:[38;5;10m[49m stop at the first one. So an embedded NUL shortens `s1`, and a leading NUL in
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    109[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `s2` empties the reject set entirely (making `strcspn` return `strlen(s1)`).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    110[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    111[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - `"a\0b\ncd\n"`: `strlen(s1)` is 1, the chop clears index 0, `s1` is empty -> `0`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    112[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - `"abc\na\0b\n"`: reject set is empty -> `3`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    113[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    114[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Pinned by `embedded_nul_bytes`, `boundary_with_nul_and_crlf`. A mutant that
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    115[0m:[38;5;10m[49m scanned the full 100-byte reject buffer instead of stopping at NUL failed 2
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    116[0m:[38;5;10m[49m tests.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    117[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    118[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### 5. `char` signedness and high bytes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    119[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    120[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `strcspn` compares raw bytes, so values `0x80..0xff` must be handled as
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    121[0m:[38;5;10m[49m unsigned. The Rust uses `u8` throughout. All 256 byte values were exercised on
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    122[0m:[38;5;10m[49m each side of the comparison (`every_byte_value`).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    123[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    124[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### 6. Output format
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    125[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    126[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `printf("%zu\n", ...)` emits an unsigned decimal with a trailing newline and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    127[0m:[38;5;10m[49m nothing else. stderr is never written; the exit status is always 0, including
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    128[0m:[38;5;10m[49m for empty input. A mutant dropping the newline failed all 14 tests; a mutant
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    129[0m:[38;5;10m[49m returning exit code 1 failed all 14.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    130[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    131[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Coverage
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    132[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    133[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `translation/tests/differential.rs`, 14 tests, none `#[ignore]`d, skipped or
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    134[0m:[38;5;10m[49m disabled:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    135[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    136[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | Test | Input class |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    137[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |---|---|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    138[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `both_binaries_run` | Phase A smoke check, both binaries produce the expected reference output |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    139[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `empty_and_near_empty_input` | empty input, `"\n"`, `"\n\n"`, `"\n\n\n"`, bare NUL — the index `-1` paths |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    140[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `single_line_no_trailing_newline` | one item; EOF with no newline; the chop eating a data byte |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    141[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `strcspn_match_positions` | match at index 0 / middle / last index / no match / empty reject set / empty `s1` |
